## 4. Joint definitions and limits

| Topic / item | Plan / execution description | Status |
|---|---|---|
| J1 base yaw | Zero points along +X. Mechanical: -160 to +160 degrees. Commanded: -150 to +150 degrees. | Confirmed |
| J2 shoulder pitch | Zero is upper arm horizontal-forward; positive raises it. Mechanical: -100 to +120 degrees. Commanded: -90 to +110 degrees. | Confirmed |
| J3 elbow pitch | Zero is a straight elbow. Bidirectional mechanical range: -145 to +145 degrees. Commanded: -140 to +140 degrees. | Confirmed; packaging validation required |
| J4 wrist pitch | Zero is tool axis collinear with the forearm. Mechanical: -140 to +140 degrees. Commanded: -130 to +130 degrees. | Confirmed |
| J5 wrist roll | Zero is nominal upright tool roll. Mechanical: -180 to +180 degrees. Commanded: -160 to +160 degrees. | Confirmed |
| G1 gripper | Derive physical limits from the gripper linkage; expose normal operation as 5-95 percent. | TBD |

## 5. Loads and performance targets

| Topic / item | Plan / execution description | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Object payload | 750 g, excluding the gripper and modular interface. | Confirmed |
| End-effector mass | Use 500 g provisionally for gripper plus interface. Initial total tool-end sizing load: 1.25 kg. | Provisional |
| Upper-arm link mass | Use 300 g provisionally for the L1 structural link, excluding the J3 motor/gearbox/encoder assembly. | Provisional |
| Forearm link mass | Use 280 g provisionally for the L2 structural link, excluding the wrist servo assembly. | Provisional |
| Cable/tubing allowance | Use 75 g provisionally on the upper arm and 75 g provisionally on the forearm. | Provisional |
| Rtelligent 42AM08 motor mass | Use 510 g per motor for torque/moving-mass calculations. J1 and J2 motor masses are near the base/shoulder; the J3 motor is included as moving mass on the upper arm. | Source-backed |
| Omron E6B2 encoder mass | Use 100 g per encoder for torque/moving-mass calculations. | Source-backed approximation |
| ST3215 servo mass | Use 70 g per servo provisionally. J4 and J5 use two servos in the wrist; G1 uses the third servo in the gripper/tool assembly. | Provisional |
| RMCS-1120 driver mass | Use 0 g moving-arm contribution because the drivers should be mounted off-arm. | Confirmed approach |
| Assumed gearbox mass | Use 450 g provisionally for the moving J3 gearbox in the torque model. J1/J2 gearbox masses are not counted as distal moving masses for J2 gravity torque. | Provisional |
| Brackets/bearings allowance | Use 200 g provisionally for the moving J3 joint brackets and bearings; wrist brackets/bearings are included in the 300 g wrist assembly. | Provisional |
| J3 moving joint assembly | Use 1.26 kg provisionally for the J3 motor, encoder, assumed gearbox, brackets and bearings. | Provisional |
| Wrist moving assembly | Use 300 g provisionally for two ST3215 servos plus wrist brackets and bearings. | Provisional |
| Total distal moving mass | Current torque model uses 3.54 kg carried by J2, including links, cables/tubing, J3 assembly, wrist assembly, tool assembly and payload. | Preliminary |
| Torque model | Include payload, gripper/interface, wrist hardware, links, actuators, cables and tubing. Do not treat 0.71 N.m holding torque as dynamic torque. | Confirmed approach |
| Accuracy and repeatability | Target +/-5 mm TCP accuracy and +/-3 mm repeatability after calibration. | Provisional |
| Joint speed | Target at least 30 deg/s for J1-J3 and 60 deg/s for J4-J5. | Provisional |
| Safety margins | Structural factor of safety 2.0; required continuous torque no more than 67 percent of available continuous output torque after efficiency. | Provisional |
| Moving-arm mass | Target 10 kg or less, excluding base, supplies and off-arm pneumatic equipment. | Provisional |
| Preliminary torque result | Current first-pass minimum output capacities: J1 = 1.45 N.m, J2 = 25.12 N.m, J3 = 9.12 N.m, J4 = 1.64 N.m, J5 = 0.51 N.m. | Preliminary |
| Gearbox screening | Initial screen: J1 at least 10:1, J2 about 100:1 or higher, J3 about 40:1 or higher. Final choice needs torque-speed curves and gearbox data. | Preliminary |
| Detailed torque file | Stored under [`analysis_artifacts/Torque_calculations.md`](analysis_artifacts/Torque_calculations.md). | Complete |
| Link-length sweep file | Stored under [`analysis_artifacts/Link_length_torque_sweep.md`](analysis_artifacts/Link_length_torque_sweep.md). | Complete |

## 6. Modular tool interface

| Topic / item | Plan / execution description | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Mechanical interface | Use repeatable datums and a positive lock. The pogo connector carries no structural load. | Confirmed approach |
| Four pogo contacts | Provisional allocation: +12 V, ground, half-duplex serial data and tool-detect/analogue-ID. | Provisional |
| Tool-change sequence | Disable power, mechanically attach/lock, detect the tool, then enable power. No hot-plugging under load. | Confirmed approach |
| Mechanical gripper | Connect the ST3215 through 12 V, ground and serial data. | Provisional |
| Soft gripper | Keep pump/regulator off-arm; use lightweight tool-side valve/control hardware and a pneumatic quick connector. | Provisional |
| Electrical capacity | Verify pogo continuous/peak current against servo and valve loads; add separately rated power contacts if required. | Validation required |

